+ - Build fix for C90 ([#284]).  The header compiles as C90; a strict
+   `-pedantic-errors` C90 compilation still reports the three
+   `utf8proc_property_t` bit-fields whose declared types are fixed by the
+   struct's binary layout.
+ - Silence ASAN warning ([#240]), CMake modernization ([#260]).
 
 ## Version 2.10.0 ##
 
@@ -35,6 +39,11 @@
  - Unicode 16 support ([#277]).
  - New `utf8proc_charwidth_ambiguous` function to return whether a character has
    East Asian width class A (Ambiguous) ([#270]).
+ - `UTF8PROC_STABLE` no longer has any effect.  Redesigning the combining table
+   moved the Unicode composition exclusions into the generated table itself, so
+   composition respects versioning stability whether or not the flag is passed,
+   and passing no flag no longer composes excluded pairs.  (Recorded
+   retroactively: this behaviour change was not noted at the time of release.)
 
 ## Version 2.9.0 ##
 
